# Direwolf config for the RX-only SDR I-Gate — TEMPLATE.
# Copy to igate.conf ON THE BOX and fill in the operator identity there.
# The real file is field config and is never committed (same rule as the
# rocket repo's callsign_binding).

# Audio arrives on stdin from rtl_fm (see the systemd unit / README pipeline)
ADEVICE stdin null
ACHANNELS 1
CHANNEL 0

# --- operator identity: FILL IN ON THE BOX, DO NOT COMMIT ---
MYCALL N0CALL-10
# APRS-IS login. Passcode derives from the callsign (well-known algorithm;
# direwolf ships a generator). Keep it out of git anyway.
IGSERVER noam.aprs2.net
IGLOGIN N0CALL 00000

# RX-only gate: no PTT, no digipeating (that's the later, TX-capable phase)
# Report the gate itself to APRS-IS (position beacon via the -IS side only).
# Fill in the station coordinates on the box; commented until then.
#PBEACON sendto=IG delay=0:30 every=60:00 symbol="igate" overlay=R lat=00^00.00N long=000^00.00W comment="Apogee field I-Gate (RX-only)"
